1
00:00:02,559 --> 00:00:11,560
Chapter 7 My first quarter at Lowwood seemed an age and not the golden age either.

2
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:15,139
It comprised an irksome struggle with difficulties in

3
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:18,799
habituating myself to new rules and unwanted tasks.

4
00:00:19,985 --> 00:00:23,920
The fear of failure in these points harassed me worse than the physical

5
00:00:23,921 --> 00:00:27,959
hardships of my lot, though these were no trifles.

6
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:35,979
During January, February and part of March, the deep snows and, after their

7
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:39,631
melting, the almost impassable roads, prevented our

8
00:00:39,632 --> 00:00:44,079
stirring beyond the garden walls, except to go to church.

9
00:00:45,129 --> 00:00:50,719
But within these limits we had to pass an hour every day in the open air.

10
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:55,340
Our clothing was insufficient to protect us from the severe cold.

11
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,139
We had no boots.

12
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:00,200
The snow got into our shoes and melted there.

13
00:01:01,219 --> 00:01:06,820
Our ungloved hands became numbed and covered with chill blades, as were our feet.

14
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:13,180
I remember well the distracting irritation I endured from this cause every evening,

15
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:18,530
when my feet inflamed and the torture of thrusting the

16
00:01:18,531 --> 00:01:21,739
swelled roar and stiff toes into my shoes in the morning.

17
00:01:23,489 --> 00:01:26,979
Then, the scanty supply of food was distressing.

18
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:31,122
With the keen appetites of growing children, we had

19
00:01:31,123 --> 00:01:34,780
scarcely sufficient to keep alive a delicate invalid.

20
00:01:35,829 --> 00:01:39,645
From this deficiency of nourishment resulted an

21
00:01:39,646 --> 00:01:42,841
abuse, which pressed hardly on the younger pupils.

22
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:47,728
Whenever the famished great girls had an opportunity, they

23
00:01:47,729 --> 00:01:50,739
would coax or menace the little ones out of their portion.

24
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:55,570
Many a time I have shared between two claimants, the

25
00:01:55,572 --> 00:01:59,139
precious morsel of brown bread distributed at tea time.

26
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:03,920
And after relinquishing to a third half the contents of my mug of coffee,

27
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:09,090
I have swallowed the remainder with an accompaniment of

28
00:02:09,091 --> 00:02:13,260
secret tears forced from me by the exigency of hunger.

29
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:18,260
Sundays were dreary days in that wintery season.

30
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:23,520
We had to walk two miles to Brockelbridge Church, where our patron officiated.

31
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,360
We set out cold.

32
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,639
We arrived at church colder.

33
00:02:28,479 --> 00:02:31,200
During the morning service we became almost paralyzed.

34
00:02:32,184 --> 00:02:37,239
It was too far to return to dinner, and an allowance of cold meat and bread,

35
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:41,121
in the same panurious proportion observed in our

36
00:02:41,122 --> 00:02:44,520
ordinary meals, was served round between the services.

37
00:02:46,014 --> 00:02:51,520
At the close of the afternoon service, we returned by an exposed and hilly road,

38
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:57,559
where the bitter winter wind, blowing over a range of snowy summits to the north,

39
00:02:58,514 --> 00:03:01,120
almost flayed the skin from our faces.

40
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:07,420
I can remember Miss Temple walking lightly and rapidly along our drooping line,

41
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:13,379
her plaid cloak, which the frosty wind fluttered, gathered close about her,

42
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:17,950
and encouraging us by precept and example to keep up our

43
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:23,159
spirits, and march forward, as she said, like stalwart soldiers.

44
00:03:24,379 --> 00:03:27,801
The other teachers poor things were generally themselves

45
00:03:27,802 --> 00:03:30,940
too much dejected to attempt the task of cheering others.

46
00:03:32,299 --> 00:03:36,920
How we longed for the light and heat of a blazing fire when we got back.

47
00:03:38,239 --> 00:03:42,239
But, to the little ones at least, this was denied.

48
00:03:42,979 --> 00:03:47,319
Each hearth in the school room was immediately surrounded by a double row of

49
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:51,516
great girls, and behind them the younger children crouched

50
00:03:51,518 --> 00:03:55,379
in groups, wrapping their starved arms in their pinnophores.

51
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:58,319
A little solace came at tea-time.

52
00:03:59,139 --> 00:04:03,979
In the shape of a double ration of bread, a hole instead of a half slice,

53
00:04:04,790 --> 00:04:07,600
with the delicious addition of a thin scrape of butter.

54
00:04:08,329 --> 00:04:14,200
It was the hebedometal treat, to which we all looked forward from Sabbath to Sabbath.

55
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:19,920
I generally contrived to reserve a moiety of this bounteous repast for myself,

56
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:24,959
but the remainder I was invariably obliged to part with.

57
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:31,100
The Sunday evening was spent in repeating, by heart, the church catechism,

58
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:38,100
and the fifth, sixth, and seventh chapters of St. Matthew, and in listening to a long

59
00:04:38,101 --> 00:04:44,540
sermon read by Miss Miller, whose irrepressible yawns attested her weariness.

60
00:04:46,159 --> 00:04:51,420
A frequent interlude of these performances was the enactment of the part of Uticus,

61
00:04:52,110 --> 00:04:57,780
by some half-dozen of little girls, who, overpowered with sleep, would fall

62
00:04:57,781 --> 00:05:04,629
down, if not out of the third loft, yet off the fourth form, and be taken up half dead.

63
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:10,219
The remedy was, to thrust them forward into the center of the school room,

64
00:05:10,790 --> 00:05:14,000
and oblige them to stand there till the sermon was finished.

65
00:05:14,719 --> 00:05:19,100
Sometimes their feet failed them, and they sank together in a heap.

66
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,840
They were then propped up with the monitors high stalls.

67
00:05:25,069 --> 00:05:30,940
I have not yet alluded to the visits of Mr. Brockelhurst, and indeed, that

68
00:05:30,941 --> 00:05:36,581
gentleman was from home, during the greater part of the first month after my arrival.

69
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:40,360
Perhaps prolonging his stay with his friend, the Archdeacon.

70
00:05:41,579 --> 00:05:43,559
His absence was a relief to me.

71
00:05:44,979 --> 00:05:50,940
I need not say that I had my own reasons for dreading his coming, but come he did

72
00:05:51,090 --> 00:05:52,090
at last.

73
00:05:53,559 --> 00:05:57,799
One afternoon, I had then been three weeks at Lowwood.

74
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:03,120
As I was sitting with a slate in my hand, puzzling over a sum in long division,

75
00:06:03,829 --> 00:06:10,620
my eyes, raised in abstraction to the window, caught sight of a figure just passing.

76
00:06:11,194 --> 00:06:14,620
I recognized almost instinctively that gaunt outline.

77
00:06:15,629 --> 00:06:21,479
And when, two minutes after, all the school teachers included rose on mass.

78
00:06:22,389 --> 00:06:25,495
It was not necessary for me to look up in order

79
00:06:25,495 --> 00:06:28,681
to ascertain whose entrance they thus greeted.

80
00:06:29,899 --> 00:06:32,579
A long stride measured the school room.

81
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:38,440
And presently beside Miss Temple, who herself had risen, stood the same

82
00:06:38,441 --> 00:06:44,120
black column, which had frowned on me so ominously from the hearth rug of Gateshead.

83
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:48,340
I now glanced sideways at this piece of architecture.

84
00:06:49,239 --> 00:06:50,840
Yes, I was right.

85
00:06:51,379 --> 00:06:56,120
It was Mr. Brockelhurst, buttoned up in a surtaught, and looking longer,

86
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,600
narrower, and more rigid than ever.

87
00:07:00,309 --> 00:07:03,479
I had my own reasons for being dismayed at this apparition.

88
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:08,780
To well, I remembered the perfidious hints given by Mrs. Reed about my disposition,

89
00:07:09,299 --> 00:07:10,299
etc.

90
00:07:11,129 --> 00:07:14,862
The promise pledged by Mr. Brockelhurst to a prize

91
00:07:14,863 --> 00:07:18,639
Miss Temple and the teachers of my vicious nature.

92
00:07:20,389 --> 00:07:23,680
All along, I had been dreading the fulfillment of this promise.

93
00:07:24,504 --> 00:07:29,500
I had been looking out daily for the coming man, whose information respecting

94
00:07:29,501 --> 00:07:34,700
my past life and conversation was to brand me as a bad child forever.

95
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:37,200
Now there he was.

96
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,879
He stood at Miss Temple's side.

97
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,379
He was speaking low in her ear.

98
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:46,159
I did not doubt he was making disclosures of my villainy.

99
00:07:46,975 --> 00:07:52,340
And I watched her eye with painful anxiety, expecting every moment to see its

100
00:07:52,341 --> 00:07:57,120
dark orb turn on me, a glance of repugnance and contempt.

101
00:07:58,790 --> 00:07:59,799
I listened, too.

102
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:02,742
And as I happened to be seated quite at the

103
00:08:02,743 --> 00:08:06,040
top of the room, I caught most of what he said.

104
00:08:06,219 --> 00:08:09,459
Its import relieved me from immediate apprehension.

105
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:16,420
I suppose, Miss Temple, the thread I bought at Loughton will do.

106
00:08:17,549 --> 00:08:21,573
It struck me that it would be just of the quality for

107
00:08:21,574 --> 00:08:25,379
the Calico Chameces and I sorted the needles to match.

108
00:08:26,479 --> 00:08:32,219
You may tell Miss Smith that I forgot to make a memorandum of the darning needles,

109
00:08:33,110 --> 00:08:35,579
but she shall have some papers sent in next week.

110
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:42,521
And she is not, on any account, to give out more than one at a time to each pupil.

111
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:47,420
If they have more, they are apt to be careless and lose them.

112
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:51,920
And oh, ma'am, I wish the woolen stockings were better looked to.

113
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:56,433
When I was here last, I went into the kitchen

114
00:08:56,434 --> 00:08:59,600
garden and examined the clothes drying on the line.

115
00:09:00,819 --> 00:09:05,219
There was a quantity of black hose in a very bad state of repair.

116
00:09:06,090 --> 00:09:08,742
From the size of the holes in them, I was sure they

117
00:09:08,743 --> 00:09:12,159
had not been well-mended from time to time, he paused.

118
00:09:13,709 --> 00:09:17,040
Your directions shall be attended to, sir, said Miss Temple.

119
00:09:18,079 --> 00:09:19,860
And ma'am, he continued.

120
00:09:20,829 --> 00:09:24,500
The lawn dress tells me some of the girls have two clean tuckers in the week.

121
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,180
It is too much.

122
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,959
The rules limit them to one.

123
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:32,540
I think I can explain that circumstance, sir.

124
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:37,799
Agnes and Catherine Johnston were invited to take tea with some friends at Loughton

125
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:42,680
last Thursday and I gave them leave to put on clean tuckers for the occasion.

126
00:09:44,479 --> 00:09:46,159
Mr. Brockelhurst nodded.

127
00:09:47,010 --> 00:09:54,159
Well, for once it may pass, but please not to let the circumstance occur too often.

128
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,180
And there is another thing which surprised me.

129
00:09:57,989 --> 00:10:04,100
I find, in settling accounts with the housekeeper, that a lunch, consisting of

130
00:10:04,101 --> 00:10:09,240
bread and cheese, has twice been served out to the girls during the past fortnight.

131
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:10,700
How is this?

132
00:10:12,030 --> 00:10:17,180
I looked over the regulations and I find no such meal as lunch mentioned,

133
00:10:18,059 --> 00:10:21,620
who introduced this innovation and by what authority?

134
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:27,700
I must be responsible for the circumstance, sir, replied Miss Temple.

135
00:10:28,659 --> 00:10:33,620
The breakfast was so ill prepared that the pupils could not possibly eat it and I

136
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:37,000
dared not allow them to remain fasting till dinner time.

137
00:10:38,219 --> 00:10:40,520
Madam, allow me an instant.

138
00:10:41,545 --> 00:10:47,059
You are aware that my plan in bringing up these girls is not to accustom them to

139
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:53,860
habits of luxury and indulgence, but to render them hardy, patient, self-denying.

140
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:59,020
Should any little accidental disappointment of the appetite occur,

141
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:05,379
such as the spoiling of a meal, the under or the overdressing of a dish,

142
00:11:06,069 --> 00:11:10,739
the incident ought not to be neutralised by replacing with something more delicate,

143
00:11:11,590 --> 00:11:18,659
the comfort lost, thus pampering the body and obviating the aim of this institution.

144
00:11:19,930 --> 00:11:25,020
It ought to be improved to the spiritual edification of the pupils by encouraging

145
00:11:25,021 --> 00:11:28,620
them to evince fortitude under the temporary privation.

146
00:11:29,649 --> 00:11:34,479
A brief address on those occasions would not be mistimed, wherein a judicious

147
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:38,899
instructor would take the opportunity of referring to the sufferings of the

148
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:44,979
primitive Christians, to the torments of martyrs, to the exhortations of our

149
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:50,040
blessed Lord Himself, calling upon His disciples to take up their cross and

150
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:56,299
follow Him, to His warnings that man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word

151
00:11:56,300 --> 00:12:01,200
that precedeth out of the mouth of God, to His divine consolations.

152
00:12:02,479 --> 00:12:07,440
If ye suffer hunger or thirst for my sake, happy are ye.

153
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:13,180
Oh, madam, when you put bread and cheese instead of burnt porridge into these

154
00:12:13,181 --> 00:12:17,040
children's mouths, you may indeed feed their vile bodies,

155
00:12:17,041 --> 00:12:20,799
but you little think how you starve their immortal souls.

156
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:27,819
Mr. Brockelhurst, again paused, perhaps overcome by his feelings.

157
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:34,940
Ms. Temple had looked down when he first began to speak to her, but she now gazed

158
00:12:34,941 --> 00:12:41,159
straight before her, and her face, naturally pale as marble, appeared to be

159
00:12:41,161 --> 00:12:44,399
assuming also the coldness and complexity of that material.

160
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:52,340
Especially her mouth closed as if it would have required a sculpt as chisel to open

161
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:57,420
it, and her brow settled gradually into petrified severity.

162
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:04,700
Meantime, Mr. Brockelhurst, standing on the hearth with his hands behind his back,

163
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,899
majestically surveyed the whole school.

164
00:13:09,030 --> 00:13:13,113
Suddenly, his eye gave a blink, as if it had met something

165
00:13:13,114 --> 00:13:17,340
that either dazzled or shocked its pupil, turning.

166
00:13:18,059 --> 00:13:21,559
He said in more rapid accents than he had hitherto used.

167
00:13:22,799 --> 00:13:29,559
Ms. Temple, Ms. Temple, what, what is that girl with curled hair, red hair ma'am

168
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:34,579
curled all over, and extending his cane, he pointed to the awful object,

169
00:13:35,139 --> 00:13:36,879
his hand shaking as he did so.

170
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:42,100
It is Julia 7 replied Ms. Temple very quietly.

171
00:13:43,479 --> 00:13:50,579
Julia 7 ma'am, and why has she or any other curled hair, why in defiance of

172
00:13:50,581 --> 00:13:56,139
every precept and principle of this house, does she conform to the world so openly,

173
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:59,772
here in an evangelical charitable establishment

174
00:13:59,773 --> 00:14:02,820
as to wear her hair one mass of curls?

175
00:14:04,190 --> 00:14:08,780
Julia's hair curls naturally, returned Ms. Temple, still more quietly.

176
00:14:09,879 --> 00:14:14,200
Naturally, yes, but we are not to conform to nature.

177
00:14:14,799 --> 00:14:19,159
I wish these girls to be the children of grace, and why that abundance.

178
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:25,940
I have again and again intimated that I desire the hair to be arranged closely,

179
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:28,040
modestly, plainly.

180
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:32,440
Ms. Temple, that girl's hair must be cut off entirely.

181
00:14:33,159 --> 00:14:34,479
I will send a barber tomorrow.

182
00:14:35,569 --> 00:14:41,739
And I see others who have far too much of the excrescence, that tall girl tell it a

183
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:48,040
turnaround, tell all the first form to rise up and direct their faces to the wall.

184
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:52,940
Ms. Temple passed her handkerchief over her lips, as if

185
00:14:52,941 --> 00:14:56,200
to smooth away the involuntary smile that curled them.

186
00:14:57,360 --> 00:15:00,811
She gave the order, however, and when the first class

187
00:15:00,813 --> 00:15:04,819
could take in what was required of them, they obeyed.

188
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:09,630
Leaning a little back on my bench, I could see the looks

189
00:15:09,631 --> 00:15:12,840
and grimaces with which they commented on this manoeuvre.

190
00:15:13,739 --> 00:15:16,579
It was a pity Mr. Brocklehurst could not see them, too.

191
00:15:17,799 --> 00:15:22,200
He would perhaps have felt that whatever he might do with the outside of the cup

192
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:27,739
and platter, the inside was further beyond his interference than he imagined.

193
00:15:28,829 --> 00:15:32,093
He scrutinized the reverse of these living medals

194
00:15:32,093 --> 00:15:35,581
some five minutes, then pronounced sentence.

195
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:38,520
These words fell like the nail of doom.

196
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,840
All those topnotes must be cut off.

197
00:15:42,879 --> 00:15:44,440
Ms. Temple seemed to demonstrate.

198
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:47,520
Madame, he pursued.

199
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:51,840
I have a master to serve whose kingdom is not of this world.

200
00:15:52,485 --> 00:15:58,879
My mission is to mortify in these girls the lusts of the flesh, to teach them to

201
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,754
clothe themselves with shame, facetness and

202
00:16:01,755 --> 00:16:05,081
sobriety, not with braided hair and costly apparel.

203
00:16:05,950 --> 00:16:09,819
And each of the young persons before us has a string of

204
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:13,579
hair twisted in plates which vanity itself might have woven.

205
00:16:14,444 --> 00:16:17,139
These, I repeat, must be cut off.

206
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:23,020
Think of the time wasted of... Mr. Brocklehurst was here interrupted.

207
00:16:23,799 --> 00:16:26,739
Three other visitors, ladies, now entered the room.

208
00:16:27,829 --> 00:16:31,520
They ought to have come a little sooner, to have heard his lecture on dress,

209
00:16:32,430 --> 00:16:36,399
for they were splendidly attired in velvet, silk and furs.

210
00:16:38,209 --> 00:16:43,959
The two younger of the trio, fine girls of 16 and 17, had gray beaver hats,

211
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:49,739
then in fashion, shaded with ostrich plumes, and from under the brim of this

212
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:55,440
graceful headdress, fell a profusion of light-tresses, elaborately curled.

213
00:16:56,170 --> 00:17:00,819
The elder lady was enveloped in a costly velvet shawl, trimmed with ermine,

214
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,239
and she wore a false front of French curls.

215
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:11,180
These ladies were deferentially received by Miss Temple, as Mrs. and the Mrs.

216
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:15,879
Brocklehurst, and conducted to seats of honour at the top of the room.

217
00:17:17,809 --> 00:17:22,680
It seems they had come in the carriage with their reverend relative, and had been

218
00:17:22,681 --> 00:17:27,860
conducting a rummaging scrutiny of the room upstairs, while he transacted

219
00:17:27,861 --> 00:17:31,054
business with the housekeeper, questioned the

220
00:17:31,055 --> 00:17:33,880
laundress and lectured the superintendent.

221
00:17:34,959 --> 00:17:40,120
They now proceeded to address divers, remarks and reproofs to Miss Smith,

222
00:17:41,110 --> 00:17:45,739
who was charged with the care of the linen and the inspection of the dormitories.

223
00:17:46,764 --> 00:17:49,340
But I had no time to listen to what they said.

224
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,100
Other matters called off and enchanted my attention.

225
00:17:55,600 --> 00:18:00,219
Hither too, while gathering up the discourse of Mr. Brocklehurst and Miss

226
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:05,559
Temple, I had not, at the same time, neglected precautions to secure my

227
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:11,960
personal safety, which I thought would be affected if I could only elude observation.

228
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:19,559
To this end, I had sat well back on the form, and while seeming to be busy with my

229
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:24,500
sum, had held my slate in such a manner as to conceal my face.

230
00:18:25,415 --> 00:18:30,719
I might have escaped notice, had not my treacherous slate somehow happened to slip

231
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:37,400
from my hand, and falling with an obtrusive crash directly drawn every eye upon me.

232
00:18:37,979 --> 00:18:42,328
I knew it was all over now, and as I stooped to pick up the

233
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:46,739
two fragments of slate, I rallied my forces for the worst.

234
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:48,540
It came.

235
00:18:50,090 --> 00:18:57,420
A careless girl, said Mr. Brocklehurst, and immediately after, it is the new pupil

236
00:18:57,421 --> 00:19:01,287
I perceive, and before I could draw breath, I must

237
00:19:01,288 --> 00:19:04,540
not forget I have a word to say respecting her.

238
00:19:05,530 --> 00:19:08,340
Then allowed, how loud it seemed to me.

239
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,680
Let the child who broke her slate come forward.

240
00:19:13,069 --> 00:19:15,360
Of my own accord, I could not have stirred.

241
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:17,260
I was paralyzed.

242
00:19:18,229 --> 00:19:24,360
But the two great girls who sat on each side of me, set me on my legs and pushed

243
00:19:24,361 --> 00:19:28,878
me towards the dread judge, and then Miss Temple gently assisted

244
00:19:28,879 --> 00:19:33,000
me to his very feet, and I caught her whispered counsel.

245
00:19:34,930 --> 00:19:37,620
Don't be afraid Jane, I saw it was an accident.

246
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,600
You shall not be punished.

247
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,819
The kind whisper went to my heart like a dagger.

248
00:19:45,079 --> 00:19:53,079
Another minute, and she will despise me for a and an impulse of fury against Reed,

249
00:19:53,579 --> 00:19:57,899
Brocklehurst, and company bounded in my pulses at the conviction.

250
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:00,360
I was no Helen Burns.

251
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:05,951
Fetch that stool, said Mr. Brocklehurst, pointing to

252
00:20:05,952 --> 00:20:09,540
a very high one from which a monitor had just risen.

253
00:20:10,299 --> 00:20:11,299
It was brought.

254
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:14,180
Place the child upon it.

255
00:20:15,094 --> 00:20:18,719
And I was placed there by whom I don't know.

256
00:20:19,899 --> 00:20:22,540
I was in no condition to note particulars.

257
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:27,940
I was only aware that they had hoisted me up to the height of Mr. Brocklehurst's

258
00:20:27,941 --> 00:20:33,639
nose, that he was within a yard of me, and that a spread of shot orange and

259
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:40,280
purple silk pelises and a cloud of silvery plumage extended and waved below me.

260
00:20:41,139 --> 00:20:42,780
Mr. Brocklehurst hemmed.

261
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:47,079
Ladies, said he, turning to his family.

262
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:50,760
Ms. Temple, teachers, and children, you all see this girl?

263
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:55,131
Of course they did, for I felt their eyes directed

264
00:20:55,132 --> 00:20:58,399
like burning glasses against my scorched skin.

265
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:01,840
You see, she is yet young.

266
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:05,100
You observe she possesses the ordinary form of childhood.

267
00:21:05,101 --> 00:21:10,379
God has graciously given her the shape that he has given to all of us.

268
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:16,159
No signal deformity points her out as a marked character.

269
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:21,719
Who would think that the evil one had already found a servant and agent in her?

270
00:21:22,930 --> 00:21:26,319
Yet such, I grieve to say, is the case.

271
00:21:27,450 --> 00:21:32,979
A pause, in which I began to steady the palsy of my nerves and to feel that the

272
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:35,820
Rubicon was passed and that the trial no

273
00:21:35,822 --> 00:21:39,480
longer to be shirked must be firmly sustained.

274
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:45,479
My dear children pursued the black marble clergyman with pathos.

275
00:21:46,444 --> 00:21:52,860
This is a sad, a melancholy occasion, for it becomes my duty to warn you that

276
00:21:52,861 --> 00:21:57,639
this girl, who might be one of God's own lambs, is a little castaway.

277
00:21:58,399 --> 00:22:03,379
Not a member of the true flock, but evidently an interloper and an alien.

278
00:22:04,399 --> 00:22:06,620
You must be on your guard against her.

279
00:22:07,239 --> 00:22:08,700
You must shun her example.

280
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:13,189
If necessary, avoid her company, exclude her from

281
00:22:13,190 --> 00:22:15,820
your sports and shut her out from your converse.

282
00:22:16,879 --> 00:22:18,760
Teachers, you must watch her.

283
00:22:19,709 --> 00:22:23,226
Keep your eyes on her movements, way well her words,

284
00:22:23,227 --> 00:22:26,920
scrutinize her actions, punish her body to save her soul.

285
00:22:27,735 --> 00:22:35,219
If indeed such salvation be possible for my tongue falters while I tell it.

286
00:22:35,899 --> 00:22:41,120
This girl, this child, the native of a Christian land, worse than many a little

287
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:44,899
heathen who says its prayers to Brahma and kneels before juggernaut.

288
00:22:45,225 --> 00:22:47,260
This girl is a liar.

289
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:54,479
Now came a pause of ten minutes, during which I, by this time in perfect

290
00:22:54,579 --> 00:23:00,159
possession of my wits, observed all the female brocklehersts produce their pocket

291
00:23:00,161 --> 00:23:06,000
hankerchiefs and apply them to their optics, while the elderly lady swayed

292
00:23:06,001 --> 00:23:12,319
herself to and fro, and the two younger ones whispered, how shocking Mr.

293
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:13,620
Brockleherst resumed.

294
00:23:14,729 --> 00:23:20,239
This I learned from her benefactress, from the pious and charitable lady who

295
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:25,639
adopted her in her orphan state, reared her as her own daughter and whose

296
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:32,739
kindness, whose generosity, the unhappy girl repaid by an ingratitude so bad,

297
00:23:33,479 --> 00:23:39,379
so dreadful, that at last her excellent patroness was obliged to separate her from

298
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:42,478
her own young ones, fearful, lest her vicious

299
00:23:42,479 --> 00:23:46,060
examples should contaminate their purity.

300
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:52,200
She has sent her here to be healed, even as the Jews of old sent their disease

301
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:58,200
to the troubled pool of Bethesda, and teachers, super-intendent,

302
00:23:58,799 --> 00:24:02,840
I beg of you not to allow the waters to stagnate round her.

303
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:09,260
With this sublime conclusion, Mr. Brockleherst adjusted the top button of

304
00:24:09,261 --> 00:24:14,559
his shirt out, muttered something to his family, who rose, bowed to Miss Temple,

305
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:18,899
and then all the great people sailed in state from the room.

306
00:24:20,139 --> 00:24:25,819
Turning at the door, my judge said, let her stand half an hour longer on that

307
00:24:25,820 --> 00:24:30,059
stool, and let no one speak to her during the remainder of the day.

308
00:24:31,579 --> 00:24:38,399
There was I then, mounted aloft, I, who had said I could not bear the shame

309
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:42,334
of standing on my natural feet in the middle of the room,

310
00:24:42,335 --> 00:24:46,299
was now exposed to general view on a pedestal of infamy.

311
00:24:47,729 --> 00:24:53,219
What my sensations were, no language can describe, but just as they all rose,

312
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:58,579
stifling my breath and constricting my throat, a girl came up and passed me.

313
00:24:59,379 --> 00:25:01,620
In passing, she lifted her eyes.

314
00:25:02,670 --> 00:25:04,840
What a strange light inspired them.

315
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:09,360
What an extraordinary sensation that race sent through me.

316
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:15,040
How the new feeling bore me up, it was as if a martyr, a hero,

317
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:19,739
had passed a slave or victim, an imparted strength in the transit.

318
00:25:20,805 --> 00:25:23,432
I mastered the rising hysteria, lifted up

319
00:25:23,433 --> 00:25:26,441
my head, and took a firm stand on the stool.

320
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:32,360
Helen Burns asked some slight question about her work of Miss Smith, was chidden

321
00:25:32,361 --> 00:25:35,790
for the triviality of the inquiry, returned to

322
00:25:35,791 --> 00:25:38,899
her place, and smiled at me as she again went by.

323
00:25:39,809 --> 00:25:40,809
What a smile.

324
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:46,479
I remember it now, and I know that it was the effluence of fine intellect,

325
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:48,000
of true courage.

326
00:25:48,719 --> 00:25:53,520
It lit up her marked liniments, her thin face, her sunken grey eye,

327
00:25:54,079 --> 00:25:56,540
like a reflection from the aspect of an angel.

328
00:25:57,530 --> 00:26:03,479
Yet, at that moment, Helen Burns wore on her arm, the untidy badge.

329
00:26:04,239 --> 00:26:09,020
Scarcely an hour ago, I had heard her condemned by miscatured to a dinner of

330
00:26:09,045 --> 00:26:14,479
bread and water on the morrow, because she had blotted an exercise in copying it out.

331
00:26:15,899 --> 00:26:18,020
Such is the imperfect nature of man.

332
00:26:19,270 --> 00:26:25,260
Such spots are there on the disc of the clearest planet, and eyes like

333
00:26:25,261 --> 00:26:28,924
misscatchards can only see those minute defects,

334
00:26:28,925 --> 00:26:32,180
and are blind to the full brightness of the orb.
